      "role": "user",
      "content": "That breakdown of the Q10 rule and the pH effect on amino groups is much better, thanks. Can you expand on the buffering capacity part? Specifically, how does a higher protein content or a different type of flour (like rye vs. bread flour) change the dough's ability to resist those rapid pH drops? I'm trying to see if I can use flour composition to offset my temperature swings.",
